WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:04.860
We're now continue
with some announcement

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:06.560
relevant to our celebration.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.320
Last week, the students in a
2016 Dr. Martin Luther King Jr.

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:13.112
IEP design seminar
assembled their installation

00:00:13.112 --> 00:00:15.770
in Memorial Lobby.

00:00:15.770 --> 00:00:17.910
We invite you to view
the exhibit from now

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:22.070
until the end of the day
tomorrow in Memorial Lobby.

00:00:22.070 --> 00:00:25.420
The 2016 all MIT
Diversity Forum is

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:29.420
scheduled for Friday,
April 29, from 8:30 a.m.

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:30.980
To 5:30 p.m.

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:34.960
The theme this year is
reflect, understand, act.

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:38.370
The keynote speaker will
be Jelani Cobb, Director

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:42.640
of Africana Studies at the
University of Connecticut.

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:44.730
Please save the date,
and we hope to see you

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:47.720
all at this wonderful event.

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:51.600
We'll conclude today's program
with the singing of the Lift

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:54.280
Every Voice and Sing.

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:57.740
We ask that you join in and sing
the first verse of the song.

00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:01.436
The lyrics are located on
the back of your program.

00:01:01.436 --> 00:01:03.852
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:12.318 --> 00:01:16.556
[SINGING]

